5. Your design question

MACD has more parts than rise bars — should everything be specified in the UI?

My answer:

✔ NO — not everything belongs in the UI.

The profitable teams expose only the high-leverage knobs, not internal MACD structure.

Expose in UI:

require_macd_rise

macd_rise_bars

Keep fixed/hidden:

MACD fast period (12)

MACD slow period (26)

MACD signal period (9)

Whether we use histogram vs line

Exact combination logic with EMA/VWAP/green-streak filters

Why:
Too many knobs = inconsistent results + difficulty debugging.
Profitable teams intentionally restrict UI controls to “daily tuning knobs” only.

Later, if desired, we can provide:

A dropdown selector like:

“MACD Mode: Standard / Fast / Aggressive”
instead of exposing the raw periods.

For now, your UI is exactly at the correct complexity.

